{title: 513 - In Heavenly Love Abiding}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb/D]In [Eb]heavenly [Cm]love abiding, [Bb7/F]No [Eb]change [Ab]my [Gm]heart [Fm]shall [Cm]fear;
[Bb/D]And safe [Eb]is such [Bb7/Ab]confiding, [Cm]For nothing [Fm]changes [Bb/D]here.
[Gm]The [Eb/Bb]storm [Ab]may [Gm]roar [Fm]without [Bb]me, [Eb]My heart may [Bb7/F]low [Ab]be [Eb]laid;
[Fm]But God [Bb]is [Gm]round about me, And [Fm]can [Eb]I be [Bb]dismayed?

Verse 2:
[Bb/D]Wherever [Eb/G]He [Cm]may guide [Fm]me, [Bb/D]No [Bb7/F]want [Eb]shall [Ab]turn [Gm]me [Fm]back;
[Bb/D]My Shepherd [Eb]is [Bb7/Ab]besided [Cm]me, And nothing [Fm]can I [Bb/D]lack.
[Gm]His [Eb/Bb]wisdom [Gm]ever [Fm]waketh, [Eb]His sight is [Bb7/F]never [Eb]dim;
[Fm]He knows [Bb]the way [Gm]He [Ab]taketh, [Gm]And I [Fm]will [Eb]walk with [Bb]Him.

Verse 3:
[Bb/D]Green [Eb]pastures [Cm]are before [Bb/D]me, [Bb7/F]Which [Eb]yet [Ab]I [Gm]have [Fm]not [Cm]seen;
[Bb/D]Bright skies [Eb]will soon [Bb7/Ab]be [Eb/G]o'er me, [Cm]Where darkest [Fm]clouds have [Bb/D]been.
[Gm]My [Eb/Bb]hope [Ab]I [Gm]cannot [Fm]measure, [Eb]My path to [Bb7/F]life [Ab]is [Eb]free;
[Fm]My Savior [Bb]has [Gm]my [Ab]teasure, [Gm]And He [Fm]will [Eb]walk with [Bb]me.
